WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
You now have a map: CVA6 is configurable RISC-V core IP;

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:10.996
configuration selects features, platform and software make a runnable system,

3
00:00:10.996 --> 00:00:14.220
and conclusions need suitable evidence.

4
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.369
Choose a path by interest.

5
00:00:16.369 --> 00:00:22.653
For architecture, read the Introduction for IP and configuration boundaries,

6
00:00:22.653 --> 00:00:27.448
then the design modules, tracing data for one instruction.

7
00:00:27.448 --> 00:00:34.062
Historical baselines, work-in-progress sections and placeholder chapters are not

8
00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:36.790
complete guides to every variant.

9
00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:43.238
For systems, start with an SDK-listed board and configuration, match versions,

10
00:00:43.238 --> 00:00:49.770
and record your environment, commands, build and boot logs, including failures.

11
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:55.640
That is your next experiment, not one already completed by this course.

12
00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:01.344
For verification, read the verif README and choose targets and tools.

13
00:01:01.344 --> 00:01:05.147
Separate tests, coverage plans and regression;

14
00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:12.092
its VCS-specific coverage-plan flow is not a promise of identical operation in other

15
00:01:12.092 --> 00:01:12.588
tools.

16
00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:19.367
Before contributing, read the repository’s current guide and choose documentation,

17
00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:22.922
a small reproduction or a test improvement.

18
00:01:22.922 --> 00:01:26.229
Preserve versions when sources disagree.

19
00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:32.677
The links lead to official materials, while these learning paths are my course

20
00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:36.976
recommendations, not an officially certified course.

21
00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:43.425
A small optional exercise is to find an MMU or PMP field and explain it in one

22
00:01:43.425 --> 00:01:46.980
configuration- and version-scoped sentence.

